TYPES.md §3.1, DECISIONS 217: a directory holding files of two packages, neither being its
own, is E2001 once per loaded package that shares it, even when both are loaded together.
-- select --
x x.y
-- project.canon --
project acme {
  canon: "0.1"
}
-- x/y/z/one.canon --
package x
-- x/y/z/two.canon --
package x.y
-- findings.txt --
error[E2001]  x/y/z/one.canon:1:9
  directory x/y/z holds files of packages x and x.y

error[E2001]  x/y/z/two.canon:1:9
  directory x/y/z holds files of packages x.y and x

2 errors, 0 warnings in 2 packages (…)
